##

00:00:00.071 --> 00:00:04.225 position:67% line:91%
Across Britain, a lot of towns and villages
have all sorts of strange, old traditions

00:00:04.225 --> 00:00:06.411 line:91%
for Bonfire Night,
on November the 5th.

00:00:06.411 --> 00:00:08.924 line:91%
Most of those traditions involve
fire, pyrotechnics,

00:00:08.924 --> 00:00:11.691 position:67% line:91%
and a significant chance of personal injury
to anyone taking part.

00:00:11.691 --> 00:00:15.590 position:69% line:91%
And I've never shown any of those traditions
on this channel before, for a few reasons.

00:00:15.590 --> 00:00:18.410 line:91%
First, most of them have
already been well-documented.

00:00:18.410 --> 00:00:21.717 position:59% line:91%
Second, a lot of the towns actually
prefer to keep their traditions quiet,

00:00:21.717 --> 00:00:24.086 line:91%
because they already deal with
too many tourists.

00:00:24.086 --> 00:00:27.029 position:56% line:91%
Like a lot of things, mass media and
easy travel have started to ruin

00:00:27.029 --> 00:00:29.761 line:91%
what might be centuries-old
practices in the towns.

00:00:29.761 --> 00:00:31.072 line:85%
And third...

00:00:31.072 --> 00:00:33.591 position:59% line:91%
Well, I've never actually been invited
to take part before.

00:00:33.591 --> 00:00:35.829 line:91%
This is Bridgwater,
in southwest England,

00:00:35.829 --> 00:00:40.084 position:77% line:91%
and today, I'll be holding a terrifying amount of
pyrotechnics directly above my head,

00:00:40.084 --> 00:00:42.755 line:91%
in a big parade with
a couple of hundred other people.

00:00:42.755 --> 00:00:44.030 position:59% line:85%
This isn't going to be a normal video,

00:00:44.030 --> 00:00:46.051 position:59% line:91%
because honestly,
I'm not really sure what happens next.

00:00:46.051 --> 00:00:48.699 line:91%
I have no script beyond this point.
They just said,

00:00:48.699 --> 00:00:51.041 line:91%
"Do you want to be in the
squibbing display?" And...

00:00:51.041 --> 00:00:52.790 line:85%
I said yes.

00:00:52.790 --> 00:00:54.442 line:85%
<c.yellow>This is a Bridgwater squib.</c>

00:00:54.442 --> 00:00:57.950 position:59% line:91%
<c.yellow>It's a Category 4 firework,
so it should only be used in displays.</c>

00:00:57.950 --> 00:01:00.077 line:91%
<c.yellow>People obviously have had
the Health and Safety training,</c>

00:01:00.077 --> 00:01:01.992 line:91%
<c.yellow>like everybody that does it
in the street tonight.</c>

00:01:01.992 --> 00:01:03.540 position:64% line:85%
<c.yellow>It's not available to the general public,</c>

00:01:03.540 --> 00:01:06.608 line:91%
<c.yellow>and this specific one is made
only for Bridgwater Carnival.</c>

00:01:06.608 --> 00:01:09.389 position:59% line:85%
<c.yellow>In here is about a pound of gunpowder.</c>

00:01:09.389 --> 00:01:11.386 line:91%
<c.colorEEEEEE>(laughs) Okay.</c>
<c.yellow>And various metallic elements.</c>

00:01:11.386 --> 00:01:14.871 line:91%
<c.yellow>So you got iron, titanium...</c>
<c.colorEEEEEE>All stuff that's gonna spark.</c>

00:01:14.871 --> 00:01:17.791 position:58% line:91%
<c.yellow>Phosphorus, lots of phosphorus metal,
so exactly right.</c>

00:01:17.791 --> 00:01:20.548 line:91%
<c.yellow>So you get the heat burning
from the gunpowder initially,</c>

00:01:20.548 --> 00:01:23.046 line:91%
<c.yellow>which heats up the metal,
and that flies, comes out,</c>

00:01:23.046 --> 00:01:26.698 position:66% line:91%
<c.yellow>and then gives you the golds, the silvers,
as the heated elements come out the top.</c>

00:01:26.698 --> 00:01:30.001 line:91%
So I'm gonna be holding
a large chunk of

00:01:30.001 --> 00:01:32.808 line:91%
flaming gunpowder and
metal dust above my head.

00:01:32.808 --> 00:01:35.230 line:91%
<c.yellow>Yeah, two feet above your head.</c>
<c.colorEEEEEE>Okay!</c>

00:01:35.230 --> 00:01:37.936 line:91%
<c.yellow>Along with 250 other people.</c>
<c.colorEEEEEE>Alright!</c>

00:01:37.936 --> 00:01:39.746 line:91%
<c.yellow>This is the cosh.</c>
<c.colorEEEEEE>This is the cosh, right.</c>

00:01:39.746 --> 00:01:42.522 line:91%
<c.yellow>As you can see, it's a
glorified broom handle, in a way.</c>

00:01:42.522 --> 00:01:44.605 position:59% line:85%
<c.yellow>It's obviously changed over the years.</c>

00:01:44.605 --> 00:01:47.189 position:64% line:91%
<c.yellow>You can see various different-shaped ones
through the back there.</c>

00:01:47.189 --> 00:01:50.000 line:91%
<c.yellow>But this one is quite old.
This one is probably...</c>

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:51.846 line:85%
<c.yellow>60-70 years old, that one.</c>

00:01:51.846 --> 00:01:53.152 line:91%
<c.colorEEEEEE>Blimey, really?</c>
<c.yellow>Yeah.</c>

00:01:53.152 --> 00:01:55.799 line:91%
<c.yellow>My dad had it from the club.
He was well off with them.</c>

00:01:55.799 --> 00:01:58.801 line:91%
<c.yellow>A lot of these get handed on
from generation to generation.</c>

00:01:58.801 --> 00:01:59.719 line:85%
Wow, okay.

00:01:59.719 --> 00:02:02.416 line:91%
So... 60-year-old cosh,
and it's having...

00:02:02.416 --> 00:02:04.704 line:85%
I mean, some explosives tied to it.

00:02:04.704 --> 00:02:05.636 line:85%
Let's do it.

00:02:05.636 --> 00:02:07.419 line:85%
<c.yellow>So, if you will hold it...</c>

00:02:07.419 --> 00:02:08.842 line:91%
<c.colorEEEEEE>Yeah.</c>
<c.yellow>Like that.</c>

00:02:08.842 --> 00:02:11.702 line:91%
<c.yellow>They were roped on
for generations.</c>

00:02:11.702 --> 00:02:14.723 line:85%
<c.yellow>But rope... tends to stretch.</c>

00:02:14.723 --> 00:02:17.740 position:61% line:91%
<c.yellow>Years ago, they used to have a banging,
which was a fire at the end.</c>

00:02:17.740 --> 00:02:21.790 position:77% line:91%
<c.yellow>Which, we can't have an aerial anymore.
We're not allowed to fire things up into the air.</c>

00:02:21.790 --> 00:02:24.692 position:59% line:91%
Okay. I mean, we are on a High Street.
It doesn't seem unreasonable(!)

00:02:24.692 --> 00:02:27.472 position:56% line:91%
<c.yellow>It's like, any of these traditional,
regional things that</c>

00:02:27.472 --> 00:02:31.296 position:64% line:91%
<c.yellow>it wouldn't be allowed if you were to ask
anywhere else in the world to do it now.</c>

00:02:31.296 --> 00:02:33.668 line:91%
<c.yellow>In England in particular,
they would not allow it.</c>

00:02:33.668 --> 00:02:35.830 position:70% line:91%
How do you keep it safe then?
'Cause obviously, there's a lot of gunpowder,

00:02:35.830 --> 00:02:37.841 line:91%
and there's gonna be crowds
around in the street.

00:02:37.841 --> 00:02:41.831 position:67% line:91%
<c.yellow>Firstly, you'll be fully kitted out in PPE.
So you'll have always full protection on.</c>

00:02:41.831 --> 00:02:43.385 line:91%
<c.yellow>When we leave here
and we line you up,</c>

00:02:43.385 --> 00:02:46.596 position:56% line:91%
<c.yellow>you'll be carrying this out
with your gloved hand over the fuse.</c>

00:02:46.596 --> 00:02:49.217 line:91%
<c.yellow>So it's held like that
over your shoulder.</c>

00:02:50.554 --> 00:02:53.884 line:91%
<c.yellow>This is a bag of lighting wads.
It's soaked in fluid.</c>

00:02:53.884 --> 00:02:55.956 position:61% line:91%
<c.yellow>Lighter fluid.</c>
<c.colorEEEEEE>Blue roll in lighter fluid. Yeah, okay.</c>

00:02:55.956 --> 00:02:57.614 line:91%
<c.yellow>We place those down
the middle of the street.</c>

00:02:57.614 --> 00:02:58.284 line:85%
Yep.

00:02:58.284 --> 00:03:01.622 position:58% line:91%
<c.yellow>And once I'm happy that
they're all in place, I sound a horn.</c>

00:03:01.622 --> 00:03:04.853 line:91%
<c.yellow>The lighters from each club
will light these wads.</c>

00:03:04.853 --> 00:03:07.957 position:66% line:91%
<c.yellow>So you'll see a seam of fire
going down through the centre of the road.</c>

00:03:07.957 --> 00:03:11.382 position:63% line:85%
<c.yellow>Then you just pull off the safety cover.</c>

00:03:11.382 --> 00:03:12.179 line:85%
Yep.

00:03:12.179 --> 00:03:14.563 line:91%
<c.yellow>And again, once those wads are lit,
down through the road,</c>

00:03:14.563 --> 00:03:17.213 line:91%
<c.yellow>and you hear the second horn...</c>
<c.colorEEEEEE>The second horn, okay.</c>

00:03:17.213 --> 00:03:18.876 line:85%
First horn, safety cover off.

00:03:18.876 --> 00:03:23.453 line:91%
<c.yellow>Yeah, all you do is dip your fuse
straight into the lighting fluid.</c>

00:03:23.453 --> 00:03:25.587 line:91%
<c.yellow>It'll fire straight away.</c>
<c.colorEEEEEE>Yep.</c>

00:03:25.587 --> 00:03:27.963 line:91%
<c.yellow>And then vertical,
up above your head at arm's length.</c>

00:03:27.963 --> 00:03:28.815 line:85%
Right.

00:03:28.815 --> 00:03:30.794 line:91%
<c.yellow>It sounds very simple,
but it will seem a lot—</c>

00:03:30.794 --> 00:03:34.990 position:69% line:91%
It doesn't sound that simple!
That's a lot of gunpowder very near my head!

00:03:34.990 --> 00:03:36.869 line:91%
<c.yellow>That is very true,
but you'll be fine.</c>

00:03:36.869 --> 00:03:40.001 position:63% line:91%
<c.yellow>You'll enjoy it, honestly,
but it will seem longer than a minute(!)</c>

00:03:40.581 --> 00:03:42.144 line:85%
<c.yellow><i>Squibbing today is historic.</i></c>

00:03:42.144 --> 00:03:45.201 position:72% line:91%
<c.yellow><i>It's been part of the tradition of Bridgwater,
going back to the 1600s.</i></c>

00:03:45.201 --> 00:03:47.429 line:85%
<c.yellow><i>Almost 430 years-ish now,</i></c>

00:03:47.429 --> 00:03:49.686 line:91%
<c.yellow><i>there's been a squibbing
of one form or another.</i></c>

00:03:49.686 --> 00:03:53.811 position:67% line:91%
<c.yellow><i>It's all to do with the 1605 Gunpowder Plot
and the failure of Guy Fawkes.</i></c>

00:03:53.811 --> 00:03:56.072 line:91%
<c.yellow><i>People had a bonfire,
they threw the effigy on it,</i></c>

00:03:56.072 --> 00:03:58.391 line:91%
<c.yellow><i>and they used to have
fireworks around the pubs.</i></c>

00:03:58.391 --> 00:03:59.573 line:85%
<c.yellow><i>And that's how it started.</i></c>

00:03:59.573 --> 00:04:01.326 line:85%
We're on the move.

00:04:01.326 --> 00:04:04.036 line:91%
<c.yellow><i>Back then, they'd make
their own fireworks at home,</i></c>

00:04:04.036 --> 00:04:07.455 position:58% line:91%
<c.yellow><i>which was lots of wads of paper,
and of course, they're very volatile.</i></c>

00:04:07.455 --> 00:04:10.344 line:91%
<c.yellow><i>A lot of them exploded.
People were killed over the years.</i></c>

00:04:10.344 --> 00:04:13.999 position:64% line:91%
<c.yellow><i>And then, groups in the pubs then started
to have a theme, they'd dress up.</i></c>

00:04:13.999 --> 00:04:18.565 position:59% line:91%
<c.yellow><i>So Carnival was born from that,
but the squibbing was the start of it.</i></c>

00:04:18.565 --> 00:04:22.735 position:61% line:91%
<c.yellow><i>And then coming right up to modern day,
post-Second World War onwards,</i></c>

00:04:22.735 --> 00:04:24.152 line:85%
<c.yellow><i>we've had organized displays.</i></c>

00:04:24.152 --> 00:04:26.965 position:63% line:91%
<c.yellow><i>Obviously, the finale after the Carnival
procession is the squibbing event.</i></c>

00:04:26.965 --> 00:04:28.315 line:85%
<c.cyan><i>Light the wads!</i></c>

00:04:28.315 --> 00:04:30.519 line:91%
<c.yellow><i>We have got the opportunity
to set a record.</i></c>

00:04:30.519 --> 00:04:33.106 line:91%
<c.yellow><i>The 400th anniversary
in 2005</i></c>

00:04:33.106 --> 00:04:36.279 line:91%
<c.yellow><i>of the failed Gunpowder Plot,
we had 180.</i></c>

00:04:36.279 --> 00:04:38.317 line:91%
<c.yellow><i>So I said,
"Let's try and get 200."</i></c>

00:04:38.317 --> 00:04:40.678 line:91%
<c.yellow><i>And the clubs have been great,
for we got 250.</i></c>

00:04:40.678 --> 00:04:42.218 line:85%
Okay, now I'm nervous.

00:04:46.362 --> 00:04:52.020 line:91%
<c.cyan><i>...from ten, nine, eight,
seven, six,</i></c>

00:04:52.020 --> 00:04:57.084 line:91%
<c.cyan><i>five, four, three,
two, one.</i></c>

00:04:57.084 --> 00:04:59.375 line:85%
<c.cyan><i>Light those squibs!</i></c>

00:05:11.278 --> 00:05:13.859 line:91%
<c.cyan><i>Stand well back,
ladies and gentlemen.</i></c>

00:05:13.859 --> 00:05:15.249 line:85%
<c.cyan><i>Make sure you're safe.</i></c>

00:05:16.766 --> 00:05:18.589 line:85%
<c.cyan><i>Absolutely fantastic!</i></c>

00:05:20.776 --> 00:05:22.533 line:91%
<c.cyan><i>And you can see these
coloured squibs.</i></c>

00:05:23.639 --> 00:05:26.617 line:91%
<c.cyan><i>You can see these
coloured squibs in the middle.</i></c>

00:05:26.617 --> 00:05:29.340 line:91%
<c.yellow><i>Squibbing is unique to Bridgwater.
It's unique to Bridgwater Carnival.</i></c>

00:05:29.340 --> 00:05:31.612 line:91%
<c.yellow><i>It's the biggest illuminated
carnival in Europe,</i></c>

00:05:31.612 --> 00:05:33.332 line:91%
<c.yellow><i>and probably second or third
in the whole world.</i></c>

00:05:33.332 --> 00:05:35.850 position:56% line:91%
<c.yellow><i>So it is something special,
and squibbing is a big part of that.</i></c>

00:05:37.132 --> 00:05:40.582 line:91%
<c.cyan><i>Thank you very much indeed,
ladies and gentlemen!</i></c>

00:05:40.582 --> 00:05:42.981 line:64%
<c.cyan><i>We sincerely hope that next year,</i></c>

00:05:42.981 --> 00:05:46.309 line:68%
<c.cyan><i>we'll have a proper Carnival
back on the streets of Bridgwater.</i></c>

